    Lines:
      Loved:
      - 'Haddock. Forty-one years and I never tired of it. You''ve a good eye.'
      Liked:
      - 'A proper fish from off the bottom. That''s kindly meant, and kindly taken.'
      Neutral:
      - 'Thank you. I''ll have it with a cup of tea and the tide table.'
      Disliked:
      - 'We used those for bait, when I was going out. Still, it''s the thought.'
